From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 5 Jun 2026 21:32:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 00683/11171] [outer-loop] Sudoku v4 amortized capstone:
 reversal confirms the wall is amortization (split verdict)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

4-way eval on the SAME trained Refiner + carved global-negative EBT (n=500, seed0):
  random-init energy descent      0.000   (v1->v3 failure, recomputed)
  refiner greedy (amortized)      0.180   (replicates v1's 0.182)
  refiner-init energy descent     0.166   (learned start, SAME energy)
  energy-rerank refiner@K=32       0.120

CONFIRMED by reversal: identical energy, only init differs -> 0.000 (cold) vs
0.166 (learned refiner init). The 0->16.6% jump from initialization alone proves
the wall was amortized inference, not the energy.

HONEST NEGATIVE: the carved EBT does NOT improve the amortized generator here —
energy polishing slightly hurts (0.18->0.166), energy-reranking K=32 hurts more
(0.18->0.12). The Langevin-carved EBT scores gross validity but cannot discriminate
among the refiner's near-correct candidates. Energy's role narrows to training
oracle + validity gate, NOT a rerank stage on a strong amortized generator.

